  "problem": "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{2x-5}{(x-5)^{2}}=\\frac{2}{x-5}+\\frac{B}{(x-5)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $B?$",
  "worked_solution": "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-5)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-5 & =2(x-5)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=5$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(5)-5 & =2(5-5)+B \\\\ 10-5 & =2(0)+B \\\\ 5 & =0+B \\\\ B & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
